From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dallas Delaney <dadelan@microsoft.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 02:43:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] erofs: consume compact v1 signed artifacts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Discover at most one signed dm-verity referrer for each platform manifest, require a matching subject and complete artifacts for every source layer, retain only the selected payloads, and reconstruct the signed EROFS tar-index data without changing unsigned behavior.

Reuse containerd’s normal content-addressed fetch and unpack paths, including deferred unpack, while binding signed snapshots to their root hash and signature identity so plain or differently signed snapshots cannot satisfy the selected materialization.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

Copilot-Session: 3ee5a7a9-81c1-4429-89fd-c54c9bcb1db6
